      {
        "id": "p64-q32-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\theta=\\dfrac{6r-2R}{R-r}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta=\\frac{6r-2R}{R-r}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use both arc lengths and the two radial boundaries: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R\\theta+r\\theta+2(R-r)=2(r\\theta+2r)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The shaded boundary contains both arcs and two radial lengths. Using $l=r\\theta$, the perimeters in centimetres are\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{APQB}&=R\\theta+r\\theta+2(R-r)\\\\P_{OAB}&=r\\theta+2r.\\end{align*}$$\nThe shaded perimeter is twice the unshaded perimeter, so\n$$\\begin{align*}(R+r)\\theta+2(R-r)&=2(r\\theta+2r)\\\\(R-r)\\theta&=6r-2R\\\\\\theta&=\\frac{6r-2R}{R-r}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q32-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $R<3r$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R<3r",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Since ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R-r>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", part (a) gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "6r-2R>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $\\theta>0$ and $R>r$, part (a) gives\n$$\\begin{align*}6r-2R&=\\theta(R-r)\\\\6r-2R&>0\\\\R&<3r.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q32-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $R>\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi+3}{\\pi+1}\\right)r$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R>\\frac{\\pi+3}{\\pi+1}r",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p64-q32-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Apply ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta<2\\pi",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " to part (a), using ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "R-r>0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The sector angle satisfies $\\theta<2\\pi$. Using part (a) and $R-r>0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6r-2R}{R-r}&<2\\pi\\\\6r-2R&<2\\pi(R-r)\\\\(2\\pi+6)r&<(2\\pi+2)R\\\\R&>\\frac{\\pi+3}{\\pi+1}r.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
